2204	\\x18b0e15f9dd74981af51a44268c9a96e0eb0ffe34b76465fa0e65eadfceaa8f8	1042	\N	D	D	The speed of sound in a material is influenced by factors such as temperature, density, and elasticity. Higher temperatures generally increase the speed of sound in gases, while higher density and elasticity in solids and liquids also increase the speed. Color, however, is a property related to light and does not affect sound propagation.	15	2025-05-28 17:54:06.73	e462f390-8633-4058-8e05-9d1edce465a0	95	270
2205	\\xc3c6f931dd9c44fab22524f023db72b0b5c1f4e59b18471b809ff7dc79a5871b	961	\N	A	A	If Earth's axis were not tilted, there would be no seasons. The tilt of Earth's axis causes different parts of the planet to receive varying amounts of sunlight throughout the year, leading to seasonal changes. Without this tilt, the climate would remain relatively constant year-round.	32	2025-05-28 17:54:06.736	e462f390-8633-4058-8e05-9d1edce465a0	95	270
2206	\\x7e65da349884465db6345abf4d99c1157a32e475b0064874aeceb94107b46581	1043	\N	B	B	Earth's axis is tilted at an angle of approximately 23.5 degrees relative to its orbital plane around the Sun. This tilt is responsible for the changing seasons as different parts of Earth receive varying amounts of sunlight throughout the year.	9	2025-05-28 17:54:06.746	e462f390-8633-4058-8e05-9d1edce465a0	95	270
2207	\\x066bbe4529f640acb14a3626fc2b495807c496853d3f40638c04f261df5a6411	962	\N	B	D	Earth rotates counterclockwise when viewed from the North Pole. This means that the Sun appears to rise in the east and set in the west. The direction of rotation is consistent with the general rotation of most planets in the Solar System.	22	2025-05-28 17:54:06.752	e462f390-8633-4058-8e05-9d1edce465a0	95	270
2208	\\x763ee326ef7341f688cd92a0677700edd568413d361f4272b99b915e150ec201	1044	\N	B	B	The Earth takes approximately 24 hours to complete one full rotation on its axis. This period is known as a solar day and is the basis for our 24-hour day. The rotation causes the cycle of day and night as different parts of the Earth face towards or away from the Sun.	14	2025-05-28 17:54:06.76	e462f390-8633-4058-8e05-9d1edce465a0	95	270
2209	\\x14e1863aee434081be7215d1a94286652ba402aad06443c6bec34f403c4be2b1	963	\N	B	B	The tilt of Earth's axis (approximately 23.5 degrees) combined with its revolution around the Sun causes the seasons. As the Earth orbits the Sun, different parts of the planet receive varying amounts of sunlight, leading to the changes in temperature and weather patterns that define the seasons.	14	2025-05-28 17:54:06.764	e462f390-8633-4058-8e05-9d1edce465a0	95	270
2210	\\x916a2c1b752a40f2a609c73a251b604d4dee73fa5fc34322a2de2925aad209bd	1045	\N	A	A	During a total solar eclipse, the Moon completely blocks the Sun's light, casting a shadow on the Earth. This results in a temporary darkness in the region where the total eclipse is visible.	29	2025-05-28 17:54:06.773	e462f390-8633-4058-8e05-9d1edce465a0	95	270
2211	\\x09e1f58d0a8047b394f84c596c5d70272aa8a95fa43c487384b98e2557bbe9f5	1046	\N	B	C	Water expands when it freezes, which is why ice has a larger volume than liquid water.	15	2025-05-28 17:57:55.291	1c777ea1-ba1b-42f8-a30b-c545ccb1389e	95	271
2212	\\x6789c3be048b449e92527f9900c866ab8fa2d0418d6948e5bd1971d78b55190c	1047	\N	A	A	Freezing is the process where a liquid turns into a solid, such as water turning into ice.	8	2025-05-28 17:57:55.303	1c777ea1-ba1b-42f8-a30b-c545ccb1389e	95	271
2213	\\xac9c6b8107894f52af607ec995b143e4600dfa3aa45342989fd1f1510f857048	1048	\N	B	B	Evaporation is the process where liquid water turns into water vapor, such as a lake drying up due to heat and lack of rainfall.	12	2025-05-28 17:57:55.316	1c777ea1-ba1b-42f8-a30b-c545ccb1389e	95	271
2214	\\x910bddad2d8d4c219cf26ea1444c924b043dab8a45df4835ba1273c8e7bd855f	1049	\N	B	B	Not conserving fuel can lead to higher energy prices due to increased demand and depletion of resources.	22	2025-05-28 17:57:55.324	1c777ea1-ba1b-42f8-a30b-c545ccb1389e	95	271
2215	\\x3e808ed88a3242649f1fdadca4175d2aca2459f3483d4c78ab9082fe96c369ef	1050	\N	C	C	Argon is a noble gas and is chemically inert, meaning it does not easily react with other substances.	21	2025-05-28 17:57:55.332	1c777ea1-ba1b-42f8-a30b-c545ccb1389e	95	271
2216	\\xcf8efc49d67348c4a8d68f5da549a705ddda713d06cb46869bedcb3b675cb43d	1051	\N	C	C	Sublimation is the process where a solid turns directly into a gas. An example is dry ice (solid CO2) turning into carbon dioxide gas.	22	2025-05-28 17:57:55.34	1c777ea1-ba1b-42f8-a30b-c545ccb1389e	95	271
2217	\\x78c421cf7629407b82438f581cb8a9ade4d19fcb33b94a5c96253898e9ebc0e7	1052	\N	C	C	Sublimation is the process where a solid turns directly into a gas. An example is dry ice (solid CO₂) turning into carbon dioxide gas.	7	2025-05-28 17:57:55.348	1c777ea1-ba1b-42f8-a30b-c545ccb1389e	95	271
2218	\\x6115e9254cde42a2ac2d6d72c5405dd00990a0a0c4c34f0dba20685f4e6bef57	1053	\N	C	C	Sublimation is the transition of a substance directly from the solid to the gas phase without passing through the liquid phase.	3	2025-05-28 17:57:55.364	1c777ea1-ba1b-42f8-a30b-c545ccb1389e	95	271
2219	\\x7205726e7fed4e43a58cb83054823ed970c903c2e5174b7a8da502dd76435fd7	1017	\N	A	A	Sublimation is the process where a solid turns directly into a gas, such as dry ice turning into carbon dioxide gas.	5	2025-05-28 17:57:55.368	1c777ea1-ba1b-42f8-a30b-c545ccb1389e	95	271
2220	\\xb397c5a0674b49aa8ab6502553a8cdd43325b850457f4dbba208e465f53f39d1	1054	\N	B	B	When a liquid becomes a gas, its particles gain energy and move farther apart, filling the available space.	13	2025-05-28 17:57:55.379	1c777ea1-ba1b-42f8-a30b-c545ccb1389e	95	271
2221	\\xefb92f74f3504c51ad9fdabf4dd11f5d53324271e6424b64821ab858d0c56b67	1055	\N	C	C	Imports allow a country to access a wider variety of goods and services that may not be available or are more expensive to produce domestically. This can lead to increased consumer choice, improved quality of life, and greater economic efficiency, as resources can be allocated more effectively.	14	2025-05-28 18:00:53.364	375ce68f-28ee-483a-ad47-49b847919417	95	272
2222	\\xb6895ef202e84626b988348970f0090b441a4ea38d914f45ad615dff1083dc3b	1056	\N	C	C	Exports can lead to increased foreign exchange earnings, which can be used to pay for imports, service foreign debt, or build up foreign reserves. This can strengthen a country's currency and improve its balance of payments, contributing to overall economic stability and growth.	9	2025-05-28 18:00:53.373	375ce68f-28ee-483a-ad47-49b847919417	95	272
2223	\\x106fcda11af147a29447537a4c53f543618125370fb0483ab903c110d8b252d4	1057	\N	C	C	The balance of trade is the difference between the value of a country's exports and imports. A positive balance (exports > imports) is called a trade surplus, while a negative balance (imports > exports) is called a trade deficit. This is a crucial indicator of a country's economic health and its position in the global economy.	8	2025-05-28 18:00:53.381	375ce68f-28ee-483a-ad47-49b847919417	95	272
2224	\\xaf37a2cd21014d3ab1031cf070a8fe5ed2c019dc3f544b49a31b50cdd53ca10d	1058	\N	B	B	A trade quota is a government-imposed limit on the quantity of a good that can be imported or exported during a specific period. This is often used to protect domestic industries from foreign competition, manage the balance of trade, or achieve other economic or political objectives. However, quotas can lead to higher prices for consumers and inefficiencies in the market.	6	2025-05-28 18:00:53.389	375ce68f-28ee-483a-ad47-49b847919417	95	272
2225	\\xa28396eee434493d8336550dff28f9dcaf04d86b12f34f35b03fb55dd08cd82e	1059	\N	B	B	A country's trade policy is designed to regulate the flow of goods and services across its borders, often with the aim of protecting domestic industries, promoting exports, and managing the balance of trade. This can involve measures such as tariffs, quotas, subsidies, and trade agreements, which can have significant impacts on the economy and international relations.	7	2025-05-28 18:00:53.402	375ce68f-28ee-483a-ad47-49b847919417	95	272
2226	\\x3d58ec95291b455b8c878e7778e2b2521b2038b84140451aaf840a22244651d8	1060	\N	B	B	A trade embargo is a government-imposed restriction on trade with a specific country, often for political or economic reasons. This can be used as a tool of foreign policy to exert pressure on a country to change its behavior, such as in cases of human rights violations or national security concerns. However, trade embargoes can also have negative economic impacts on both the imposing and target countries.	5	2025-05-28 18:00:53.41	375ce68f-28ee-483a-ad47-49b847919417	95	272
2227	\\x783b3ee4891c44a0827d8fe3e488eaf08591ab416b8e47d0b983dc0f7e3eb081	1061	\N	A	A	A key disadvantage of a sole trader business is limited access to capital. Sole traders often rely on personal savings and loans, which can be insufficient for significant business expansion compared to partnerships or corporations that can raise funds from multiple investors.	7	2025-05-28 18:00:53.418	375ce68f-28ee-483a-ad47-49b847919417	95	272
2228	\\x4023e74b43364667ac27dea64a5d479f62df2ae6f3c249fcadee979662cddaa1	1062	\N	C	C	Information asymmetry occurs when one party in a transaction has more or better information than the other. This can lead to market inefficiencies such as adverse selection (as in insurance markets) and moral hazard (as in principal-agent relationships).	10	2025-05-28 18:00:53.427	375ce68f-28ee-483a-ad47-49b847919417	95	272
2229	\\xcf0aa505d6ce465f8c8fe106203975804e502b57e91d401ea314811a1133903b	1063	\N	B	B	Relying heavily on exports can make a country vulnerable to global economic downturns, as a decrease in global demand for its goods and services can lead to reduced export revenues, lower economic growth, and potential job losses. This highlights the importance of economic diversification to mitigate risks associated with external shocks.	7	2025-05-28 18:00:53.435	375ce68f-28ee-483a-ad47-49b847919417	95	272
2230	\\xdd8e63f58c3e4eebb9b99f9d683d2b0413800aabc7ef457ab8429f33d7218bc2	1064	\N	B	B	High taxation can lead to reduced incentives for work and investment. When taxes are high, individuals and businesses may have less disposable income and lower returns on investment, which can discourage work effort and investment in productive activities. This can potentially lead to slower economic growth and reduced economic efficiency.	6	2025-05-28 18:00:53.447	375ce68f-28ee-483a-ad47-49b847919417	95	272
2231	\\xb26f60bfe1534dbf83eb7723b2d374b7bf1548dc551741ca803d3d70c0ce03b3	1065	\N	B	B	To find the net force, subtract the smaller force from the larger force. Here, 10 N (push) - 5 N (pull) = 5 N. The net force is 5 N in the direction of the push, as the push force is greater.	21	2025-05-28 18:03:26.596	1f17c60b-e1b7-40c2-a0c5-ce737f3ac43b	95	273
2232	\\xf27b9e58cd0a439483b592c6f6a9c5554d23afb8771b457b861daac7404cfebb	1066	\N	C	A	A screw jack is a device that uses the principle of the inclined plane to lift heavy objects. The screw jack consists of a screw (which is essentially an inclined plane wrapped around a cylinder) and a handle. When the handle is turned, the screw rotates, and the inclined plane converts the rotational motion into linear motion, lifting the load. The mechanical advantage of a screw jack is determined by the pitch of the screw and the length of the handle.	9	2025-05-28 18:03:26.607	1f17c60b-e1b7-40c2-a0c5-ce737f3ac43b	95	273
2233	\\xef87a688ec2241ac893b223269652e668d2027d86f5647c1bc9fa56d9c33b8fa	1067	\N	C	C	The wheel and axle is a simple machine that amplifies rotational force. It consists of a wheel attached to a smaller axle. When force is applied to the wheel, it rotates the axle, transmitting rotational motion and force. This machine is commonly found in devices like steering wheels, doorknobs, and windlasses. The mechanical advantage is determined by the ratio of the radius of the wheel to the radius of the axle, allowing for efficient force amplification.	12	2025-05-28 18:03:26.616	1f17c60b-e1b7-40c2-a0c5-ce737f3ac43b	95	273
2234	\\x1535d384b1ce471cb763c2c7d13ae152f6b3d014f50043ee8d33fc0dcc1ae1cd	1068	\N	C	C	A screw is a simple machine that converts rotational motion into linear motion. It is essentially an inclined plane wrapped around a cylinder. The primary function of a screw is to hold objects together, as seen in screws used in woodworking, machinery, and construction. The threads of the screw provide a mechanical advantage by increasing the distance over which the force is applied, allowing for a strong hold.	22	2025-05-28 18:03:26.625	1f17c60b-e1b7-40c2-a0c5-ce737f3ac43b	95	273
2235	\\x33903c4df44841c0b629a7865cfbe05106ef2a7d191545cba7850340e72bb10d	1069	\N	B	B	Speakers use magnets to convert electrical signals into sound. When an electrical signal passes through the speaker's coil, it creates a magnetic field that interacts with the permanent magnet in the speaker. This interaction causes the coil to move, which in turn moves the speaker cone, producing sound waves.	8	2025-05-28 18:03:26.632	1f17c60b-e1b7-40c2-a0c5-ce737f3ac43b	95	273
2236	\\x71b254c5c96a497f98fe9749d40c84436928298082b148508e205a8cc4b350e3	1070	\N	C	C	Magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) machines use powerful magnets to produce detailed images of the body's internal structures. The magnets create a strong magnetic field that aligns the protons in the body's hydrogen atoms. Radio waves are then used to disturb this alignment, and the signals emitted by the protons as they realign are used to create detailed images.	7	2025-05-28 18:03:26.641	1f17c60b-e1b7-40c2-a0c5-ce737f3ac43b	95	273
2237	\\x8aa5a572135d4c83815a5deb4212128c42382cc131b04e5ab1632c6f767dce61	1071	\N	C	C	An MRI (Magnetic Resonance Imaging) machine uses powerful magnets to produce detailed images of the inside of the human body. The magnets create a strong magnetic field that aligns the protons in the body's hydrogen atoms. Radio waves are then used to disturb this alignment, and the signals emitted by the protons as they realign are used to create detailed images.	7	2025-05-28 18:03:26.652	1f17c60b-e1b7-40c2-a0c5-ce737f3ac43b	95	273
2238	\\xfa69408705c3470da5ae9258a5ba4011e383be5e70d74722b25bada9b2257080	1072	\N	C	C	Cardboard is an opaque material that blocks light completely, making it ideal for creating sharp and well-defined shadows in shadow puppetry. Clear plastic and frosted glass allow light to pass through, while tissue paper is translucent and scatters light, resulting in less distinct shadows.	8	2025-05-28 18:03:26.66	1f17c60b-e1b7-40c2-a0c5-ce737f3ac43b	95	273
2239	\\x56080c700f864e858ec132f7d6167286f98b88b93c544194b20e841ef97fb5f9	1073	\N	B	B	Rowing a boat involves both push and pull forces. When you pull the oars towards you, you are applying a pull force. When you push the oars away from you, you are applying a push force. This combination of forces propels the boat forward.	9	2025-05-28 18:03:26.672	1f17c60b-e1b7-40c2-a0c5-ce737f3ac43b	95	273
2240	\\xa339fb3607434ee283d052dbdc71626ceefe7dc41fca4b25a2f1654b5a7d6e7b	958	\N	B	B	The penumbra is the outer part of a shadow where the light source is only partially blocked. This results in a less dark shadow compared to the umbra. During a solar eclipse, observers in the penumbra see a partial eclipse.	8	2025-05-28 18:03:26.676	1f17c60b-e1b7-40c2-a0c5-ce737f3ac43b	95	273
2241	\\x1d6ab77b149343d7b143a3cbdf70b1a250b09e6a90484880840047e393169b99	1074	\N	C	A	Metals are malleable, meaning they can be hammered or rolled into thin sheets. They are also good conductors of electricity and have high melting points.	9	2025-05-28 18:10:36.092	818849f2-dcce-4126-a7aa-66cadecc0f4e	95	274
2242	\\x29501fc26ccd4222ade7e16cbff9e7f4272c105ae1944d86bb2031c09a67fc7c	1075	\N	C	C	Milk is a liquid because it takes the shape of its container and has a definite volume.	3	2025-05-28 18:10:36.104	818849f2-dcce-4126-a7aa-66cadecc0f4e	95	274
2243	\\xfd4d54b638d14cb881eaf6471d8716796a8535b0fc264d16921ea909d2263d53	1076	\N	C	B	Conduction is the transfer of heat through direct contact between particles. When a metal spoon is placed in hot tea, heat is transferred from the tea to the spoon through conduction. The other options involve radiation (Option 1 and 2) and convection (Option 4).	18	2025-06-01 10:00:34.818	e1993b27-37b6-4651-933d-6e2ef0a0ba19	100	275
2244	\\x3488c8247e7f4c6da6c6939149765a438b19946588cc4dbe93e5d7af97ecab3d	1077	\N	C	C	Heat is a form of energy, and its SI unit is the Joule (J). Kelvin, Celsius, and Fahrenheit are units of temperature, not heat.	4	2025-06-01 10:00:34.84	e1993b27-37b6-4651-933d-6e2ef0a0ba19	100	275
2245	\\xd4c8e816335747bbb4bf255d1957f5be96e8807b3b9a4f0e9a75136185f758ba	1078	\N	A	C	Thermostats in heating systems often use bimetallic strips that bend with changes in temperature. This bending action is used to open or close electrical circuits, thereby controlling the heating system based on the temperature.	10	2025-06-01 10:00:34.851	e1993b27-37b6-4651-933d-6e2ef0a0ba19	100	275
2246	\\x50f9320330034348bae259fae9a441c2110eaf8e3a874cef8abdb1dc9481133e	1079	\N	D	D	Thermal contraction occurs when a material decreases in size as its temperature decreases. A metal ring shrinking when cooled is an example of this phenomenon, as the metal atoms lose kinetic energy and move closer together.	15	2025-06-01 10:00:34.861	e1993b27-37b6-4651-933d-6e2ef0a0ba19	100	275
2247	\\x815876f911324f168a1b6bead0595d703903877db19d46a7bdfdabfb8043620e	1080	\N	A	B	Heat refers to the total energy transferred due to a temperature difference, which is related to the total kinetic energy of particles. Temperature, however, is a measure of the average kinetic energy of the particles in a substance.	9	2025-06-01 10:00:34.872	e1993b27-37b6-4651-933d-6e2ef0a0ba19	100	275
2248	\\x591f3f9e7ecd4a4088600c98ca42e738a7ae44ecead04e5e882a4dc1793d6059	1081	\N	C	C	Solar energy is a renewable source of heat energy because it is derived from the sun, which is an inexhaustible source of energy. Unlike coal, natural gas, and petroleum, which are fossil fuels and finite, solar energy can be harnessed continuously without depletion.	3	2025-06-01 10:00:34.881	e1993b27-37b6-4651-933d-6e2ef0a0ba19	100	275
2249	\\x3c246f4dafc94013ab13fc0773ec0da72187d04b4e2d4a39b82b5dcfa771b185	1082	\N	D	D	All the processes listed involve the transfer of heat. Heat causes the metal rod to expand, ice to melt, and the thermometer to register a temperature change. Heat transfer is a fundamental aspect of these phenomena.	8	2025-06-01 10:00:34.892	e1993b27-37b6-4651-933d-6e2ef0a0ba19	100	275
2250	\\x3d06d31aec0a4979b7eb25d9f2b2fd5eb004d26e382e408c880e99dd9e834249	1083	\N	B	C	Geothermal energy is derived from the heat stored within the Earth's core. This heat originates from the planet's formation and the radioactive decay of minerals. It is a sustainable and renewable source of energy that can be harnessed for heating and electricity generation.	15	2025-06-01 10:00:34.904	e1993b27-37b6-4651-933d-6e2ef0a0ba19	100	275
2251	\\x85c356f8d12f418b9786042ec64fd8ec50cce10571984263b09eb7a2eb833b39	1084	\N	A	D	Heat is a form of energy transfer between systems due to a temperature difference, measured in Joules. Temperature, on the other hand, is a measure of the average kinetic energy of the particles in a substance, measured in Kelvin, Celsius, or Fahrenheit. The key difference is that heat is energy in transit, while temperature is a property that indicates the thermal state of a substance.	16	2025-06-01 10:00:34.914	e1993b27-37b6-4651-933d-6e2ef0a0ba19	100	275
2252	\\x89496f1a4fdc45458f9ad18938cf7762f4db9b3972ae4d05a82dde5c92465393	1085	\N	B	D	Thermal contraction is the phenomenon where a material contracts when cooled. A balloon shrinking when cooled is an example of this, as the air inside the balloon loses kinetic energy and the molecules move closer together, reducing the volume of the air and causing the balloon to shrink.	24	2025-06-01 10:00:34.923	e1993b27-37b6-4651-933d-6e2ef0a0ba19	100	275
